%% Title: State · source gate status
%% Summary: The runtime status of one registry source, as GET /api/sources, the health drawer and the scheduler see it, and what moves a source between statuses.
%% Sources: src/config/source-registry.js (GATE_STATUSES, sourceStatus, killReason, openRoutes, routesAwaitingApproval, namedApproval, isGatedRoute), src/collectors/status.js (registryFields, isOnline, RUNTIME_STATUSES), src/collectors/refusal.js (refusalGate, envReset), src/collectors/state.js, src/collectors/governance.js (recordGateTransitions), scripts/source-admin.js; migrations 018, 020, 035, 056. Spec: TECHNICAL_SPEC.md section 17; ADR 0001 (gate status, kill switches, the blocked 4, the refused state, D1); PR #22 decision G5 (named approval).
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  [*] --> disabled : fresh clone, COLLECTOR_CONTACT_URL empty (D1), every source except the blocked 4

  state "disabled" as disabled
  state "awaiting_key" as awaiting_key
  state "awaiting_approval" as awaiting_approval
  state "awaiting_licence" as awaiting_licence
  state "blocked" as blocked
  state "collecting" as collecting
  state "blocked_by_source" as blocked_by_source

  disabled --> collecting : contact URL set and a route open (a keyless route, or a gated route with its env set and a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY)
  disabled --> awaiting_key : contact URL set, closedStatus awaiting_key
  disabled --> awaiting_approval : contact URL set, closedStatus awaiting_approval
  disabled --> awaiting_licence : contact URL set, closedStatus awaiting_licence
  [*] --> blocked : auth kind blocked, no permission route open or awaiting approval (reported even without COLLECTOR_CONTACT_URL)

  awaiting_key --> collecting : free key set in env and a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY
  awaiting_approval --> collecting : the route's required env set (approval ref, credentials or dataset path, or the operator ack for a permission-gated feed) and a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY
  awaiting_licence --> collecting : the route's required env set (licence ref and/or key or credentials, or the operator ack for a permission-gated feed) and a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY
  blocked --> collecting : the official permission env recorded (Tencent, Telegram, ResearchGate, Cato), the contact URL set and a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY
  blocked --> disabled : a kill switch, or the permission env recorded while COLLECTOR_CONTACT_URL is empty

  collecting --> disabled : env kill switch (COLLECTORS_ENABLED=false, COLLECTORS_DISABLED, SOURCE_SLUG_ENABLED=false) needs a container recreate
  collecting --> disabled : database kill switch (source-admin disable, needs GATE_APPROVED_BY), applies before the next run
  state kill_cleared <<choice>>
  disabled --> kill_cleared : kill switch cleared (source-admin enable, needs GATE_APPROVED_BY, or the env switch removed), and the registry gate decides the status again
  kill_cleared --> collecting : contact URL set and a route open
  kill_cleared --> awaiting_key : contact URL set, no route open, closedStatus awaiting_key
  kill_cleared --> awaiting_approval : contact URL set, no route open, closedStatus awaiting_approval
  kill_cleared --> awaiting_licence : contact URL set, no route open, closedStatus awaiting_licence
  kill_cleared --> blocked : auth kind blocked, no permission route open or awaiting approval
  kill_cleared --> blocked_by_source : a route open, but its refusal cooldown or probe is still pending
  kill_cleared --> disabled : COLLECTOR_CONTACT_URL empty, or another kill switch still set
  collecting --> blocked_by_source : 401, 403, 451, bot challenge or robots disallow, cooldown 1 h doubling to 24 h
  blocked_by_source --> collecting : cooldown over and the one probe run succeeds
  blocked_by_source --> blocked_by_source : probe refused again, cooldown doubles
  blocked_by_source --> collecting : SOURCE_SLUG_RESET date on or after the refusal and not in the future with a valid GATE_APPROVED_BY, or source-admin reset (needs GATE_APPROVED_BY)

  state collecting {
    direction LR
    [*] --> not_online
    not_online --> online : a successful run in the last hour, not older than the last error
    online --> not_online : an error since, or no success for an hour
  }

  note right of blocked_by_source
    runtime only (status.js), never online,
    one critical source_refused alert per episode,
    resolved when the state clears
  end note
  note left of awaiting_approval
    Reddit today, until Reddit approves the app,
    all four REDDIT_* variables are set and
    GATE_APPROVED_BY names the approver.
    G5: a gated route configured without a valid
    GATE_APPROVED_BY ("Name YYYY-MM-DD") keeps the
    source in its closed status (a blocked source
    stays blocked) with the reason
    "awaiting named approval"; removing the
    approval closes an open gated source again
  end note

  note left of disabled
    source-admin commands (scripts/source-admin.js):
    npm run source:disable -- slug --reason why
    npm run source:enable -- slug
    npm run source:reset -- slug --note why
    each needs GATE_APPROVED_BY, its recorded actor;
    every gate change is appended to source_gate_events
  end note

  note right of collecting
    legend: all done (every element is on master)
  end note

  classDef done fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,color:#1b3d1f
  class disabled, awaiting_key, awaiting_approval, awaiting_licence, blocked, collecting, blocked_by_source done
